-**Performance:** The method is optimal for the triangulation of a single polygon but can be computationally expensive for polygons with a large number of vertices. It is suitable for isopolygons on octree nodes, which typically have a manageable number of vertices [G].
-**Strengths:** Produces the minimal area triangulation for the given polygon, reducing visual artifacts compared to non-optimal triangulations. It is well-behaved for isopolygons on convex bodies [S1, S3, unofficial].
